# LF in the repository, always, for everything text.
#
# THIS EXISTS BECAUSE OF verify.sh. Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout by default, and a shell script committed with CRLF fails on the
# Linux box and in CI as `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` -- an error that names
# neither the file nor the real cause, and which nobody debugging a red build
# guesses is about line endings. The bot is written on Windows and runs on
# Ubuntu, so this is not a hypothetical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are the ones that actually break, so they say it outright
# rather than relying on the rule above still being there later.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
